<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<reference xml:id="class.streamexception" role="class" xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

 <title>The StreamException class</title>
 <titleabbrev>StreamException</titleabbrev>

 <partintro>

  <section xml:id="streamexception.intro">
   &reftitle.intro;
   <simpara>
    A <exceptionname>StreamException</exceptionname> is thrown when a stream
    operation reports a terminating error and the
    <link linkend="context.stream.error-mode"><parameter>error_mode</parameter></link>
    stream context option is set to <constant>StreamErrorMode::Exception</constant>.
   </simpara>
   <simpara>
    The exception message is the message of the first error of the operation.
    All errors of the operation are available from
    <methodname>StreamException::getErrors</methodname>.
   </simpara>
   <note>
    <simpara>
     The exception code is an internal number that may change between
     PHP versions. To identify the error, use the
     <link linkend="streamerror.props.code">code</link> property of the
     errors returned by <methodname>StreamException::getErrors</methodname>.
    </simpara>
   </note>
  </section>

